;; posix's process and file functions (PY6e; Modules/posixmodule.c): stat_result with its float and nanosecond
;; times, scandir and DirEntry, the descriptors' functions (dup2, pread, readv, inheritable and blocking flags),
;; the processes' (waitpid, wait3, wait4, execv, execve, system, times, uname), sysconf, confstr and pathconf over
;; musl's tables, statvfs, the terminal's few (isatty from the device's major number). posix has no fork: Go's
;; runtime is multithreaded, so pyi starts children only through _posixsubprocess.fork_exec (Go's ForkExec), and
;; test.support's has_fork_support is False (the class no-fork).

